From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:50:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d: Defer the activation of minimized device
 windows.

When a minimized fullscreen window is restored, it may get activated before
it is restored. wined3d then set the display mode and resized the window
while it was still minimized, and the restore brought back the size of the
desktop mode set on deactivation, e.g. 3072x1728 instead of 800x600 for Star
Wars Galactic Battlegrounds.

Don't activate minimized windows: the WM_SIZE of the restore posts
WM_ACTIVATEAPP again, which then activates the device.

diff --git a/dlls/wined3d/device.c b/dlls/wined3d/device.c
index c2630c8..193a08c 100644
--- a/dlls/wined3d/device.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/device.c
@@ -5749,7 +5749,13 @@ LRESULT device_process_message(struct wined3d_device *device, HWND window, BOOL
          * (e.g. Deus Ex: GOTY) to destroy the device, so take care to
          * deactivate the implicit swapchain last, and to avoid accessing the
          * "device" pointer afterwards. */
-        if (!wparam || !wined3d_get_activate_processed(window))
+        /* A minimized window may get activated before it is restored, the
+         * window changes would then apply to the minimized window and be lost
+         * on restore. Wait for the WM_SIZE of the restore, which activates the
+         * device again. */
+        if (wparam && IsIconic(window))
+            TRACE("Window %p is minimized, deferring activation.\n", window);
+        else if (!wparam || !wined3d_get_activate_processed(window))
         {
             wined3d_set_activate_processed(window, !!wparam);
             while (i--)
